79,2790,1372,315,4115,279,30161,14476,1817,1899,25,1019,256,481,576,1156,7216,8471,518,220,24,264,744,624,256,481,576,1537,7216,8471,518,220,21,281,744,624,256,481,576,2790,10350,882,374,504,220,24,264,744,13,311,220,21,281,744,2572,892,374,220,24,4115,4192,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe owners of the Luray Caverns in Virginia conduct tours every 20 minutes. Each day in April the first tour is at 9 a.m., and the last tour starts at 6 p.m. How many tours are there per day in April?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine the number of tours conducted per day at the Luray Caverns in April, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of hours the tours operate each day:**\n   - The first tour starts at 9 a.m.\n   - The last tour starts at 6 p.m.\n   - The total operating time is from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m., which is 9 hours.\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"46d7a28b1260b5f0baa8a34d4f674374695e4c24a4e785ed80ef3fb4130331d0"},"seconds":18.437490463256836,"seed":848218633426243484,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the number of tours conducted per day at the Luray Caverns in April, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of hours the tours operate each day:**\n   - The first tour starts at 9 a.m.\n   - The last tour starts at 6 p.m.\n   - The total operating time is from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m., which is 9 hours (from 9 to 18 in 24-hour format).\n\n2. **Calculate the number of tours in those 9 hours:**\n   - Tours are conducted every 20 minutes.\n   - Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, in 9 hours there are \\(9 \\times 60 = 540\\) minutes.\n   - The number of tours in 540 minutes, given each tour is 20 minutes apart, is \\( \\frac{540}{20} = 27 \\).\n\n3. **Verify the timing of the first and last tours:**\n   - The first tour at 9 a.m. is the 1st tour.\n   - The last tour at 6 p.m. should be the 27th tour, as it starts exactly 540 minutes (9 hours) after the first tour.\n\nTherefore, the number of tours conducted per day in April is \\(\\boxed{27}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{27}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":true},"graded_text":"To determine the number of tours conducted per day at the Luray Caverns in April, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of hours the tours operate each day:**\n   - The first tour starts at 9 a.m.\n   - The last tour starts at 6 p.m.\n   - The total operating time is from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m., which is 9 hours (from 9 to 18 in 24-hour format).\n\n2. **Calculate the number of tours in those 9 hours:**\n   - Tours are conducted every 20 minutes.\n   - Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, in 9 hours there are \\(9 \\times 60 = 540\\) minutes.\n   - The number of tours in 540 minutes, given each tour is 20 minutes apart, is \\( \\frac{540}{20} = 27 \\).\n\n3. **Verify the timing of the first and last tours:**\n   - The first tour at 9 a.m. is the 1st tour.\n   - The last tour at 6 p.m. should be the 27th tour, as it starts exactly 540 minutes (9 hours) after the first tour.\n\nTherefore, the number of tours conducted per day in April is \\(\\boxed{27}\\).","id":"algebra:932"}
